  "interpretationLimits": [
    "Overall FAIL is preserved; the macOS full suite includes a retry and is not clean, and strict macOS repetitions fail 2 of 3.",
    "Previous runs' original failures and raw evidence remain under separate run IDs; no retries, thresholds, physics, worker policy, or Git state were changed by the monitoring subagent.",
    "Each raw metrics file is a byte-identical copy of the matching original artifact file; derivatives do not alter source values.",
    "The pool timing is coordinator dispatch-to-completed-results wall time. Shard timing is separately reported compute time. Their difference combines communication, validation, main-thread and OS/browser scheduling; no exact attribution is possible from these existing coarse counters.",
    "hardwareConcurrency=3 on hosted macOS corresponds to one worker under the existing capacity policy; Ubuntu and Windows report 4 and use two workers.",
    "Playwright's desktop Chrome user agent may identify Windows on macOS/Ubuntu. Host OS is determined from CI job metadata.",
    "The original gate is p95 < 12 ms over 24 distinct completed frames, not an individual-sample limit. overBudgetRows are diagnostic samples >=12 ms and do not introduce a different gate.",
    "Empty captured LongTasks arrays do not rule out short main-thread work or scheduling delays; final LongTask assertions were not reached in attempts that failed the earlier p95 assertion.",
    "Docker workflow does not print the exact accepted shutdown code. Browser listening/audio output, subjective localization, and Docker Desktop hot reload on other machines are outside this hosted verification."
  ]
